Permission profile: {{.Profile}}
{{if .YOLO}}Sandbox mode: yolo — commands run unconfined with the full host
environment and no approval prompts; file tools may reach any path.
{{end}}
{{if .ReadOnly}}Sandbox mode: read-only — the workspace root is not writable
(OS-enforced; writes outside the explicit writable paths fail). Known
read-only commands (ls, cat, grep, git status/diff/log, ...) run without
approval; every other command asks the user.
{{end}}
{{if .ApprovedPrefixes}}Approved command prefixes: {{.ApprovedPrefixes}}
{{end}}Commands outside the approved allowlist ask the user for approval
(allow once / always allow / deny; "always allow" rules are persisted to
the project .opencraft/approvals.yaml).
File reads and writes are confined to the workspace root; paths outside
it are rejected without asking.
